From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: qcom,smp2p: add wakeup-source

A remote processor reports a crash through SMP2P. Allow wakeup-source on
an SMP2P edge, so that such a crash wakes the system up while it is
suspended, rather than at the next resume.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
Built with W=1 and dtbs_check; not tested on the device yet.

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,smp2p.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,smp2p.yaml
index f912768..770a7ff 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,smp2p.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/qcom/qcom,smp2p.yaml
@@ -59,6 +59,12 @@ properties:
     description:
       Two identifiers of the inbound and outbound smem items used for this edge.
 
+  wakeup-source:
+    description:
+      Wake the system up when the remote processor changes an inbound entry,
+      so that a crash of the remote processor is handled while the system is
+      suspended rather than at the next resume.
+
 patternProperties:
   "^master-kernel|slave-kernel|ipa-ap-to-modem|ipa-modem-to-ap|wlan-ap-to-wpss|wlan-wpss-to-ap$":
     type: object
